1
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:45,190
Within 20 miles of the Wakiva River system, there are over 2 million people, so it really is a little oasis among the populated areas of Orlando.

2
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:52,190
Behind the Wild and Scenic Rivers Act was to maintain rivers in their natural state for future generations.

3
00:00:52,190 --> 00:01:01,190
So by having a National Wild and Scenic River status, we are really showing our commitment as a community to keep this river

4
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:05,190
and its natural state for perpetuity.

5
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:12,640
This is such a remarkable place.

6
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:20,530
This river is only one out of two wild and scenic rivers in Florida.

7
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:27,530
You get in the kayak and head downstream and see some of the most pristine wild Florida,

8
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:33,530
the alligators, the turtles, the bald eagles, the cranes.

9
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:38,530
Just the wildlife in itself is just remarkable.

10
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:51,530
What it feels like when I'm in my kayak and I'm just pushing out to get out into the river is excitement, just pure delight.

11
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:55,530
I just wish more people could experience it.

12
00:01:55,530 --> 00:02:00,530
The river system really does offer something for everyone.

13
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:08,530
Whether you just want to swim and cool off or just put your feet in the water or you like to paint or take pictures

14
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:20,530
or just find some solitude and relax by the river or float on the river or whatever it is that helps you get through your day to day life.

15
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:26,530
I imagine the river system has some way to help you restore yourself.

16
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:32,530
Someone with little or no outdoor experience actually has lots of opportunities in the Wakiva system.

17
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:38,530
On top of the things that you do and or associated with the river, there are dozens of miles of hiking trails

18
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:46,530
that take you close to the river, through the sandhills, through the scrub habitats on numerous different parks.

19
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:52,530
Being a national wild and scenic river kind of puts a spotlight on the Wakiva.

20
00:02:52,530 --> 00:03:01,530
I think probably the main way you protect a resource like the Wakiva river is people need to care about it

21
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:07,530
and probably the best way to do that is to get them out on the river.

22
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:14,530
Especially young folks get them out early and let them experience some good times on the river

23
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:19,530
and that way they value it more as adults.

24
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:28,530
I just couldn't imagine Central Florida without Wakiva Springs and Kelly Park and Rock Springs.

25
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:33,530
I mean it's just ingrained in this area, this Central Florida area.

26
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:39,530
We need to protect it for not only this generation, next generation, but for future generations.

27
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:51,210
I highly recommend that people come to the river and just sit and listen and watch

28
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:59,210
and listen to the birds and watch the river roll by and feel the vibration,

29
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:03,210
meditate, hum, sing, dance.

30
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:12,210
It's all about giving thanks for being alive and you really feel being alive when you're outside.

31
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:18,210
I think people are amazed that this exists in Central Florida

32
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:23,210
and that if they haven't heard of it before they're surprised, they haven't heard of it

33
00:04:23,210 --> 00:04:29,210
and if they have heard of it before they're kind of wondering why they hadn't come out sooner and explored it.

34
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:36,210
So I think we feel disconnected somehow and we've been told that we're maybe disconnected from nature

35
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:41,210
but I would say that that is not true, that we're all connected.

36
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:50,210
If you live here, your water is spring water so we're all involved and invested whether we think we are or not.

